{
  "title": "78: al-Nabaa النبإ",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nعَمَّ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۚ‏(1)\nA’MMA YATA-SAAA-ALOON. \nOf what do they ask one another? \nعَنِ النَّبَاِ الْعَظِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nA’NIN NABA-IL A’ZEEMIL \nAbout the great event, \nالَّذِىْ هُمْ فِيْهِ مُخْتَلِفُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nLAZEE HUM FEEHE MUKHTALEFOON. \nAbout which they differ? \nكَلَّا سَيَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nKALLAA SA-YA’LAMOONA. \nNay! they shall soon come to know \nثُمَّ كَلَّا سَيَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(5)\nSUMMA KALLAA SAYA’LAMOON. \nNay! Nay! they shall soon know. \nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ الْاَرْضَ مِهٰدًا ۙ‏(6)\nALAM NAJ-A’LIL ARZA MEHAADANW. \nHave We not made the earth an even expanse? \nوَّالْجِبَالَ اَوْتَادًا ۙ‏(7)\nWAL JEBAALA AWTAADANW \nAnd the mountains as projections (thereon)? \nوَّخَلَقْنٰكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا ۙ‏(8)\nWA KHALAQNAAKUM AZWAAJANW. \nAnd We created you in pairs, \nوَّجَعَلْنَا نَوْمَكُمْ سُبَاتًا ۙ‏(9)\nWA JA-A’LNAA NAWMAKUM SOBAATANW. \nAnd We made your sleep to be rest (to you), \nوَّجَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ لِبَاسًا ۙ‏(10)\nWA JA-A’LNAL LAYLA LEBAASANW. \nAnd We made the night to be a covering, \nوَّجَعَلْنَا النَّهَارَ مَعَاشًا‏(11)\nWA JA-A’LNAN NAHAARA MA-A’ASHANW. \nAnd We made the day for seeking livelihood. \nوَّبَنَيْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعًا شِدَادًا ۙ‏(12)\nWA BANAYNAA FAWQAKUM SAB-A’N SHEDAADANW. \nAnd We made above you seven strong ones, \nوَّ جَعَلْنَا سِرَاجًا وَّهَّاجًا ۙ‏(13)\nWA JA-A’LNAA SERAAJANW WAH-HAAJANW. \nAnd We made a shining lamp, \nوَّاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ الْمُعْصِرٰتِ مَآءً ثَجَّاجًا ۙ‏(14)\nWA ANZALNAA MENAL MO’SERAATE MAAA-AN SAJJAAJAL. \nAnd We send down from the clouds water pouring forth abundantly, \nلِّنُخْرِجَ بِهٖ حَبًّا وَّنَبَاتًا ۙ‏(15)\nLE-NUKHREJA BEHI HABBANW WA NABAATANW \nThat We may bring forth thereby corn and herbs, \nوَّجَنّٰتٍ اَلْفَافًا ؕ‏(16)\nWA JANNAATIN ALFAAFAA. \nAnd gardens dense and luxuriant. \nاِنَّ يَوْمَ الْفَصْلِ كَانَ مِيْقَاتًا ۙ‏(17)\nINNA YAWMAL FASLE KAANA MEEQAATANY. \nSurely the day of decision is (a day) appointed: \nيَّوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَتَاْتُوْنَ اَفْوَاجًا ۙ‏(18)\nYAWMA TUNFAKHO FIS SOORE FA-TAATOONA AFWAAJANW. \nThe day on which the trumpet shall be blown so you shall come forth in hosts, \nوَّفُتِحَتِ السَّمَآءُ فَكَانَتْ اَبْوَابًا ۙ‏(19)\nWA FOTEHATIS SAMAAA-O FA KAANAT ABWAABANW. \nAnd the heaven shall be opened so that it shall be all openings, \nوَّ سُيِّرَتِ الْجِبَالُ فَكَانَتْ سَرَابًا ؕ‏(20)\nWA SUYYERATIL JEBAALO FA KAANAT SARAABAA. \nAnd the mountains shall be moved off so that they shall remain a mere semblance. \nاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ كَانَتْ مِرْصَادًا ۙ‏(21)\nINNA JAHANNAMA KAANAT MIRSAADAL. \nSurely hell lies in wait, \nلِّلطّٰغِيْنَ مَاٰبًا ۙ‏(22)\nLIT-TAAGHEENA MA-AABAL. \nA place of resort for the inordinate, \nلّٰبِثِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَحْقَابًا ۚ‏(23)\nLAABESEENA FEEHAA AHQAABAA. \nLiving therein for ages. \nلَا يَذُوْقُوْنَ فِيْهَا بَرْدًا وَّلَا شَرَابًا ۙ‏(24)\nLAA YAZOOQOONA FEEHAA BARDANW WA LAA SHARAABAA. \nThey shall not taste therein cool nor drink \nاِلَّا حَمِيْمًا وَّغَسَّاقًا ۙ‏(25)\nILLAA HAMEEMANW WA GHASSAAQAA. \nBut boiling and intensely cold water, \nجَزَآءً وِّفَاقًا ؕ‏(26)\nJA-ZAAA-ANW WEFAAQAA. \nRequital corresponding. \nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ حِسَابًا ۙ‏(27)\nINNAHUM KAANOO LAA YARJOONA HESAABANW. \nSurely they feared not the account, \nوَّكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا كِذَّابًا ؕ‏(28)\nWA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA KIZZAABAA. \nAnd called Our communications a lie, giving the lie (to the truth). \nوَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ اَحْصَيْنٰهُ كِتٰبًا ۙ‏(29)\nWA KULLA SHAY-IN AHSAYNAAHO KETAABAA. \nAnd We have recorded everything in a book, \nفَذُوْقُوْا فَلَنْ نَّزِيْدَكُمْ اِلَّا عَذَابًا‏(30)\nFA-ZOOQOO FALAN NAZEEDAKUM ILLAA A’ZAABAA. \nSo taste! for We will not add to you aught but chastisement. \nاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ مَفَازًا ۙ‏(31)\nINNA LIL MUTTAQEENA MAFAAZAA. \nSurely for those who guard (against evil) is achievement, \nحَدَآئِقَ وَاَعْنَابًا ۙ‏(32)\nHADAAA-EQA WA A-A’NAABANW \nGardens and vineyards, \nوَّكَوَاعِبَ اَتْرَابًا ۙ‏(33)\nWA KAWAA-E’BA ATRAABANW. \nAnd voluptuous women of equal age; \nوَّكَاْسًا دِهَاقًا ؕ‏(34)\nWA KAASAN DEHAAQAA. \nAnd a pure cup. \nلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا وَّلَا كِذّٰبًا ۚ‏(35)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA FEEHAA LAGHWANW WA LAA KIZZAABAA. \nThey shall not hear therein any vain words nor lying. \nجَزَآءً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ عَطَآءً حِسَابًا ۙ‏(36)\nJA-ZAAA-AM MIR RABBEKA A’TAAA-AN HESAABAR. \nA reward from your Lord, a gift according to a reckoning: \nرَّبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا الرَّحْمٰنِ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مِنْهُ خِطَابًا ۚ‏(37)\nRABBIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAR RAHMAANE LAA YAMLEKOONA MINHO KHETAABAA. \nThe Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, the Beneficent Allah, they shall not be able to address Him. \nيَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الرُّوْحُ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ صَفًّا ؕۙ لَّا يَتَكَلَّمُوْنَ اِلَّا مَنْ اَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَقَالَ صَوَابًا‏(38)\nYAWMA YAQOOMUR ROOHO WAL MALAAA-EKATO SAFFAL, LAA YATAKALLAMOONA ILLAA MAN AZENA LAHUR RAHMAANO WA QAALA SAWAABAA. \nThe day on which the spirit and the angels shall stand in ranks; they shall not speak except he whom the Beneficent Allah permits and who speaks the right thing. \nذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمُ الْحَقُّ ۚ فَمَنْ شَآءَ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ مَاٰبًا‏(39)\nZAALEKAL YAWMUL HAQQ, FAMAN SHAAA-AT TAKHAZA ELAA RABBEHI MA-AABAA. \nThat is the sure day, so whoever desires may take refuge with his Lord. \nاِنَّاۤ اَنْذَرْنٰكُمْ عَذَابًا قَرِيْبًا ۖۚ  يَّوْمَ يَنْظُرُ الْمَرْءُ مَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدٰهُ وَيَقُوْلُ الْكٰفِرُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ كُنْتُ تُرٰبًا‏(40)\nINNAA ANZARNAAKUM A’ZAABAN QAREEBAN-Y, YAWMA YANZORUL MAR-O MAA QADDAMAT YADAAHO WA YAQOOLUL KAAFERO YAA LAYTANEE KUNTO TORAABAA.\nSurely We have warned you of a chastisement near at hand: the day when man shall see what his two hands have sent before, and the unbeliever shall say: O! would that I were dust! ",
  "merits": "There are 40 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah everyday will be fortunate enough to visit Masjidul Haraam in the same year. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that memorization of this Surah carries great reward.\nIf this Surah is recited with the intention of staying awake, then the reciter will not fall asleep and if it is recited before travelling then the journey will become easy. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures stomach problems."
